    "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nHonor `CheckpointConfig.ckpt_fully_parallel_load_per_rank_objects` when constructing the fully parallel checkpoint loader. With `fully_parallel_load=True` and this option enabled, Bridge currently constructs Core's strategy with `per_rank_object_load=False`, silently retaining the global object-exchange policy.\n\n# Changelog\n\n- Forward the inherited option to `FullyParallelLoadStrategyWrapper` in the native distributed checkpoint loader.\n- Cover both option values with the real Core wrapper constructor, preserving the existing process group and cached strategy.\n\nSupported trigger: Bridge pretraining/resume using `torch_dist` checkpoints and fully parallel loading. The path runs through setup, the checkpoint manager, `_load_checkpoint_from_path`, `_load_base_checkpoint`, and `_load_global_dist_base_checkpoint`.\n\nCore already implements per-rank object reads in NVIDIA/Megatron-LM#5551. Its MLM entrypoint forwards this option; Bridge's separate caller omitted it. The default remains `False`. Existing config documentation is inherited from Core; no API or checkpoint format changes are introduced.\n\n# Validation\n\nRecorded Bridge base: `7983b66cfbac13b95c8edcbfe378de803b7e7516`.\nPinned Core used in tests: `8949def81eb744b9219e2d794c80265928c40a5b`.\nUpstream Core discovery base: `a3e1f8259dab053e772c8a4fb373e77ae5973b7f`.\n\nThe identical CPU regression command, using native package imports and the real Core strategy constructor:\n\n```bash\nuv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/training/test_checkpointing.py -k global_checkpoint_load_forwards_per_rank_objects -q -p no:cacheprovider\n```\n\n- Unmodified production base plus test only: exit 1; the `True` case failed with `assert False is True`, while the `False` control passed.\n- After the fix: exit 0; 2 passed.\n\nAdjacent validation:\n\n```bash\nuv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/training/test_checkpointing.py -k 'TestLoadBaseCheckpoint or TestCheckpointPathOverride or TestCheckpointDpCpGroup or checkpoint_group_includes_gtp or load_model_weights_fully_parallel_load' -q -p no:cacheprovider\nuv run pre-commit run --all-files\n```\n\nAdjacent tests: exit 0, 26 passed. All-files pre-commit: exit 0, no file modifications.\n\n`uv run mypy --strict src/megatron/bridge/training/checkpointing.py tests/unit_tests/training/test_checkpointing.py` exited 2 with the same mypy 2.2.0 internal error on the unchanged base and patched files; no type-check pass is claimed. Distributed checkpoint values, collective execution, and performance were not measured. This regression verifies the configuration-to-strategy contract.\n\n# GitHub Actions CI\n\nCI will be requested for the submitted commit. This PR remains Draft pending normal CI and maintainer review.\n\n# Before your PR is \"Ready for review\"\n\n- [x] Contributor guidelines reviewed.\n- [x] Regression and adjacent tests added/run as described above.\n- [x] Documentation evaluated: existing inherited option documentation describes the restored behavior.\n- [x] Optional dependency imports unchanged.\n\n# Additional Information\n\nPrimary area: `area:ckpt`. Type: bug fix.\n\nAll-state duplicate searches in both repositories covered the option and strategy symbols, per-rank object loading, fully parallel loading, and the observed failure. Bridge #3207 covers saving, Bridge #3832 covers per-rank save metadata, Core #5556/#4628 cover tensor replica locality, and Core #6858 covers RNG shard identity; none fixes this caller omission.\n",
